    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d56-a1">

                <pb facs="0058" n="52" sameAs="frus:frus1901China/pg52"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure No. 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to Prince Ching, Li Hung Chang,
                    etc.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-11-19"><hi rendition="#italic">November 19,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Highness and Your Excellency</hi>: I have
                    learned that General Tung Fu-hsiang is still remaining with the court.</p>
                <p>In view of the important part which he has taken in the recent events, I consider
                    that it is no place for him there, and he ought to be sent away at once.</p>
                <p>I avail myself, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. H. Conger.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
